Report a top-level parameter block's space in its sub-object range.

ExtendedTypeLayoutContext (source/slang/slang-reflection-api.cpp) records, for each parameter
group, a sub-object range whose spaceOffset spReflectionTypeLayout_getSubObjectRangeSpaceOffset
returns. It reads the variable's SubElementRegisterSpace index only when `kind`, the resource kind
the group's binding range is reflected as, is SubElementRegisterSpace. For a top-level parameter
block `kind` is a descriptor kind, so the space is never read: two ParameterBlock globals beside a
loose global, which occupy spaces 1 and 2 (their descriptor sets say so), both report 0.

This reads the variable's SubElementRegisterSpace index, or its RegisterSpace index where the
container starts a space, whatever kind the binding range is reflected as. A regression test is
added as tools/slang-unit-test/unit-test-parameter-block-space-offset.cpp.

Measured on v2026.21 (win-x64): 0 and 0 for blocks in spaces 1 and 2.
diff --git a/source/slang/slang-reflection-api.cpp b/source/slang/slang-reflection-api.cpp
index 35e27ab..0057478 100644
--- a/source/slang/slang-reflection-api.cpp
+++ b/source/slang/slang-reflection-api.cpp
@@ -2224,13 +2224,20 @@ struct ExtendedTypeLayoutContext
             subObjectRange.bindingRangeIndex = bindingRangeIndex;
             subObjectRange.offsetVarLayout = createOffsetVarLayout(typeLayout, path);
             subObjectRange.spaceOffset = 0;
-            if (kind == LayoutResourceKind::SubElementRegisterSpace && path.primary)
+            // The space a parameter block occupies is the variable's index for the space it is laid
+            // out in: `SubElementRegisterSpace` where the target gives the block a space of its own
+            // inside its parent, `RegisterSpace` where the container starts one. `kind` above is
+            // the kind the binding range is reflected as, which for a top-level block is a
+            // descriptor kind, so it is not the test of whether the block has a space.
+            //
+            if (path.primary)
             {
-                if (auto resInfo = path.primary->var->FindResourceInfo(
-                        LayoutResourceKind::SubElementRegisterSpace))
-                {
+                auto resInfo =
+                    path.primary->var->FindResourceInfo(LayoutResourceKind::SubElementRegisterSpace);
+                if (!resInfo)
+                    resInfo = path.primary->var->FindResourceInfo(LayoutResourceKind::RegisterSpace);
+                if (resInfo)
                     subObjectRange.spaceOffset = resInfo->index;
-                }
             }
             // It is possible that the sub-object has descriptor ranges
             // that will need to be exposed upward, into the parent.
